---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-attentive";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Attentive: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Evaluate Attentive for messaging after Yotpo\u2019s retirement, with documented Reviews and Loyalty integrations and explicit ownership for every customer message.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does moving to Attentive mean removing Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo documents integrations connecting Reviews and Loyalty data to Attentive. Confirm the configuration and message owners for the retained products before launch."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Attentive only an SMS replacement?",
    "answer": "No. Its current pricing page includes text and email packages. Decide whether to migrate both channels or keep email elsewhere, and budget the resulting stack explicitly."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Yotpo messaging is no longer an alternative</h2>
      <p>Yotpo scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its live notice now states that the application is decommissioned, with dashboard access and background services inactive. This comparison cannot recommend staying on Yotpo messaging for a smaller list or favorable bundle. Yotpo named Attentive as a migration partner; that makes it a relevant candidate rather than proof of fit for every store.</p>
      <h2>Attentive can cover email as well as SMS</h2>
      <p>Attentive’s current pricing page includes email and text packages, alongside other channel options. The old framing of an SMS-only destination misses the choice between migrating both channels and keeping a separate email provider. Inventory welcome, cart, review requests and promotional sends by channel. If email stays elsewhere, assign its automation ownership before connecting SMS; one customer profile does not automatically coordinate two independent senders.</p>
      <h2>Keep Reviews with a documented data route</h2>
      <p>Yotpo documents an Attentive Reviews integration for using review data in SMS and email. That offers a way to retain Yotpo Reviews while replacing messaging. Inspect customer matching and a sample review event before using reviewer-based targeting. Decide whether review collection remains with the active Reviews setup or uses a supported destination workflow; activating both request paths can create duplicate asks.</p>
      <h2>Loyalty integration changes the migration scope</h2>
      <p>Yotpo documents an Attentive Loyalty and Referrals integration, including rewarding email or SMS signup. Decide which enrollment and reward rules should remain active, then rehearse a new signup and an existing member record. Confirm that rewards are not issued twice and that a missing or outdated points field cannot produce a misleading message. Migrating the sender does not require rebuilding the whole loyalty program, but the integration needs its own acceptance check.</p>
      <h2>Recover records without promising dashboard access</h2>
      <p>Use prior exports, existing suppression records and Shopify data you can legitimately access. The retired dashboard is not a dependable export route. Establish what historical consent evidence and message assets you already hold and what support can recover. For SMS, identify the sender and consent migration requirements with the destination before launch. Do not turn every historic customer phone number into a marketable SMS subscriber.</p>
      <h2>Quote the channel mix you intend to run</h2>
      <p>Attentive says pricing can depend on messages, subscriber list, channels and premium AI tools. Obtain a scope covering the intended email/SMS split, peak sends, onboarding and retained Yotpo modules. Avoid unsupported annual minimums or claims that physical stores are required to justify the product. A retail capture program should rehearse its actual signup path; an online-only store should evaluate its own forms and lifecycle journeys rather than pay for an imagined retail future.</p>
      <h2>Launch against a message ownership map</h2>
      <p>Prepare replacement welcome and recovery messages disabled, inspect consent and purchase exclusions, and identify who can pause each automation. Confirm that active Reviews requests and Loyalty notices still have an owner after messaging changes. Attentive is a relevant choice when its channel package and documented Yotpo data routes match the program. This is a source-based evaluation plan, not a claim that we measured migration speed, compliance outcomes or attributed revenue.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Product information checked November 25, 2026. <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo migration partners</a> · <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> · <a class="link" href="https://support.yotpo.com/docs/integrating-yotpo-reviews-with-attentive">Reviews integration</a> · <a class="link" href="https://support.yotpo.com/docs/integrating-yotpo-loyalty-referrals-with-attentive">Loyalty integration</a> · <a class="link" href="https://www.attentive.com/pricing">Attentive pricing</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript">Yotpo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-attentive">Omnisend vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">Email apps for fashion stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Questions about this comparison" />
</BaseLayout>
